context:
Spike scope: run the gateway on the owner's Mac against the existing broker, with a temporary client file and isolated agent state, and the pinned omp Linux reviewer in a local Linux container. Apple `container` and Mocker are available locally (an earlier note that no Linux container was available was wrong).

Checks:
- A: scope (401, 404 Unknown model, 403 on /v1/usage);
- B: every role alias resolves through the gateway;
- C: every fallback provider (openai-codex, muse-code, google-antigravity) completes through the gateway;
- D: the fallback walk happens through the gateway;
- E: one end-to-end runner.review at @smol;
- F: reach (environ and config hold only the gateway token, fetch refused, AGENTS.md not injected).

The needs are sequencing only. D1 does not depend on evidence path semantics; the only overlap with the response slices is OMP_OVERLAY_TEXT.

Owner-only steps after a GO: the launchd gateway, tailscale serve, an ACL limiting tag:oracle-ci to the gateway port, and the OMP_GATEWAY_TOKEN secret. Then delete the old reviewer secrets and rotate the broker token, API keys and Claude setup token once, after cutover (owner decision 2026-10-22).
